WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.118
How long does your team spend looking for a screwdriver?

00:00:05.398 --> 00:00:08.224
Multiply that by every operator, every shift.

00:00:08.824 --> 00:00:14.641
When tools live in piles and drawers, people waste time searching, tools go missing,

00:00:14.641 --> 00:00:17.204
and nobody notices until a job stops.

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:21.754
Drawers also hide damaged tools until the moment someone needs them.

00:00:22.354 --> 00:00:25.375
A pegboard puts every tool on view, at the station.

00:00:25.655 --> 00:00:31.632
Its quarter-inch holes take standard hooks and holders: screwdriver holders, Allen key holders,

00:00:31.632 --> 00:00:33.645
spanner trays and slotted hooks.

00:00:33.925 --> 00:00:38.910
Hang the most-used tools at eye level, and a missing tool shows up as an empty spot.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:43.986
Group tools by task, so the operator's hand moves in one natural direction.

00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:51.060
Furnisys pegboards mount on Link Uprighters and Flexi columns, in 18 or 30 inch heights,

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.267
with 12 inch options on Flexi.

00:00:53.547 --> 00:00:56.959
Add a marker board for instructions right beside the tools.

00:00:57.559 --> 00:00:59.825
Visible tools get used and returned.

00:01:00.105 --> 00:01:02.241
What is the tool your team loses most?

00:01:02.521 --> 00:01:06.474
Comment below, and next, see how bin rails speed up picking parts.

00:01:07.074 --> 00:01:11.319
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

